accessWidener v2 official

# Goal lists on vanilla mobs, so a fox can be taught to hunt a creature.
#
# Fabric offers no API for adding a goal to a mob it does not own, and the two ways in are a mixin
# or this. An access widener is the smaller change: it grants exactly two fields and leaves every
# vanilla method body untouched, where a mixin injects into registerGoals and has to be kept working
# across versions and against every other mod injecting into the same place.
#
# The namespace is `official` rather than `named`: Minecraft has shipped unobfuscated since 26.1, so
# there is no separate named namespace left for Loom to remap this through.
#
# 26.2 added a public Mob#getGoalSelector(), so the first line is belt-and-braces — but targetSelector
# still has no accessor, and widening both keeps the two reads symmetrical at the call site.
accessible field net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob goalSelector Lnet/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/GoalSelector;
accessible field net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob targetSelector Lnet/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/GoalSelector;

# The sound engine's buffer cache, so synthesised creature voices can be handed to it directly.
#
# Creature calls are generated as PCM at runtime (see dev.jsz.primordia.sound), and there is no way
# to give the game a sound that did not come out of a resource pack — SoundEngine#play resolves an
# event through sounds.json and then asks SoundBufferLibrary for the decoded ogg. Reaching the cache
# lets a voice be seeded under the identifier the engine is about to look up, so it finds the samples
# already there and never goes to disk. Everything downstream of that point is vanilla: the same 3D
# attenuation, the same category sliders, the same pausing.
#
# The alternative was to ship a Vorbis encoder, write oggs into a runtime resource pack and force a
# resource reload every time a new creature was seen, which is slower, hitches the game, and adds a
# dependency to avoid three lines.
#
# All three are client-only classes. On a dedicated server they are never loaded and these entries
# simply never apply.
accessible field net/minecraft/client/sounds/SoundManager soundEngine Lnet/minecraft/client/sounds/SoundEngine;
accessible field net/minecraft/client/sounds/SoundEngine soundBuffers Lnet/minecraft/client/sounds/SoundBufferLibrary;
accessible field net/minecraft/client/sounds/SoundBufferLibrary cache Ljava/util/Map;
